# X API keyword search — ask first

X API is **pay-per-use** (Posts: Read ≈ **$0.005 per returned post**). MCP and CLI share the same credit pool.

## Requires explicit user approval before running

- `npx … xurl search …` / `xurl search …`
- Raw `GET /2/tweets/search/recent` (or any keyword recent-search)
- MCP `search_posts_all` (full-archive; also App-Only — usually 403 on our OAuth session)

When you want a keyword search, **stop and ask**: proposed query, approx `max_results`, and rough cost (`$0.005 × N`). Do not run until the user approves.

## OK without extra approval (prefer these)

- MCP `get_posts_by_id` / `get_posts_by_ids`
- MCP `get_users_by_username` → `get_users_posts` on known accounts
  (prefer the coldcard-hack-research **quiet-period** poll — `glxyresearch`
  first, community accounts only when hunting leads; add **situational**
  accounts only when the task needs them — see that skill’s `reference.md`)
- Other non-search read tools already in use for research

Prefer targeted MCP lookups over keyword search whenever possible. Do not
routine-poll one-shot reporters every research pass.
